MakeHuman
---------
assets/characters/human/ (the human base body, its eyes, teeth, tongue,
brows and lashes, the default humanoid's model Humanoid.glb made from
them, the skin textures in its skins/ folder, the hairstyles in its hair/
folder and the garments in its wardrobe/ folder) is made from MakeHuman's
base mesh, targets and system assets
(http://www.makehumancommunity.org), released under CC0 1.0 Universal by
their copyright holders: Data Collection AB, Joel Palmius and Jonas
Hauquier. CC0 asks for no attribution; the MakeHuman project and its
community are credited here with thanks.

The garments and hairstyles shipped here were converted from MakeHuman's
system assets and the MakeHuman community's asset packs
(https://static.makehumancommunity.org/assets/assetpacks.html). Every one
shipped in this repository is released under CC0 1.0 Universal by its
author (only items whose own file and whose pack both say CC0 are taken:
assets/characters/human/take_library.py); each keeps its author in its
manifest's "source" and in the CREDITS.md beside the items
(assets/characters/human/wardrobe/CREDITS.md and hair/CREDITS.md). They
were re-posed, re-skinned to the Axcenity Humanoid skeleton and given the
body's shapes; their textures are unchanged.

These assets were made with MPFB (https://static.makehumancommunity.org/mpfb.html),
the MakeHuman Plugin For Blender by Joel Palmius and the MakeHuman
community, licensed GPL-3.0-or-later. MPFB is used as a tool: no MPFB or
MakeHuman source code is included in this repository or in anything built
from it (assets/characters/human/README.md, "Sources and credit").

Quaternius
----------
assets/characters/human/HumanoidAnimations.glb holds 84 animations from
the Universal Animation Library and the Universal Animation Library 2 by
Quaternius (https://quaternius.com), released under CC0 1.0 Universal.
They were brought onto the human base's skeleton
(assets/characters/human/mocap.py) and renamed; the table of names is
in that file. CC0 asks for no attribution; Quaternius is credited here
with thanks.
